/*******************************************************************
*  block   : fifoctrl0
*  register: txfifoctrl0
*  field   : txthreshold0
*  access  : read-write
*
* The field indicates the threshold which is used by APP_FIFO before
* reading out the data from TX_FIFO and sending it to MAC. When the FIFO
* Fill level is equal to or greater than the Threshold value or EOF is
* seen, then the FIFO is read out and sent to MAC.  To Avoid deadlock,
* this value should never be greater than the (FIFO_DEPTH-
* SEL_AFULLTHRESH-N_ADDITIONAL_TXVALIDS).  Here, FIFO_DEPTH = Depth of
* the FIFO associated with Ch#0, SEL_AFULLTHRES = Selected Almost Full
* Threshold for Ch#0 and N_ADDITIONAL_TXVALIDS = Number of Additional
* Valids that APP Logic generates after the assertion of TxAfull on
* Ch#0.
* 
*******************************************************************/
